  "retries": "The SDK resends a 408, 409, 429 or 5xx. The facade answers a permanent 409 as 400, so it is not resent. A plain upsert, patch or delete resent after a 5xx writes the same rows again. A conditional or by-filter write is keyed (M274): its first attempt gets a native idempotency key (M132), remembered by this server for the same body, and a resend (x-stainless-retry-count above 0) sends that key, so it applies at most once and answers the first attempt's outcome. A resend this server cannot match (another server, a restart, more than 4,096 bodies since, or keys off below PSTORE_APPLIED_WRITES=3) is refused 400 retry_outcome_unknown, never evaluated again."
